==================== 3. move: copy, then delete from the source ====================

$ mkdir -p data/inbox/2026 data/site-a/processed && echo 'uploaded report' > data/inbox/upload-1.txt && echo 'uploaded slide' > data/inbox/2026/upload-2.txt

$ rclone move data/inbox data/site-a/processed -v
2026/11/01 16:47:44 INFO  : Local file system at data/site-a/processed: Server side directory move failed - fallback to file moves: can't copy directory - destination already exists
2026/11/01 16:47:44 INFO  : upload-1.txt: Moved (server-side)
2026/11/01 16:47:44 INFO  : 2026/upload-2.txt: Moved (server-side)
2026/11/01 16:47:44 INFO  : 2026: Set directory modification time (using DirSetModTime)
2026/11/01 16:47:44 INFO  : 
Transferred:   	         31 B / 31 B, 100%, 0 B/s, ETA -
Checks:                 0 / 0, -, Listed 3
Renamed:                2
Transferred:            2 / 2, 100%
Server Side Moves:      2 @ 31 B
Elapsed time:         0.0s


$ rclone lsf -R data/inbox   # files are gone from the source, the empty 2026/ folder stays
2026/

$ rclone lsf -R data/site-a/processed
2026/
upload-1.txt
2026/upload-2.txt
# --delete-empty-src-dirs also removes the emptied source folders

$ echo 'late upload' > data/inbox/2026/upload-3.txt

$ rclone move data/inbox data/site-a/processed -v --delete-empty-src-dirs
2026/11/01 16:47:45 INFO  : Local file system at data/site-a/processed: Server side directory move failed - fallback to file moves: can't copy directory - destination already exists
2026/11/01 16:47:45 INFO  : 2026: Set directory modification time (using SetModTime)
